      "author_association": "OWNER",
      "body": "## Scope\n\nExtend `factory dispatch` with a review-only intake that discovers open, non-draft pull requests explicitly opted in by either the `needs-review` label or a pending review request for the authenticated factory account. Record the PR number and current head SHA so the same revision is not reviewed twice. This lane must accept ordinary contributor branches and must not require the `agent/<issue>` naming convention.\n\n## Touches\n\n- `factory/dispatch.py`: PR discovery and dispatch entry point\n- `factory/config.py` and `factory/templates/factory.toml`: opt-in review settings only if existing authenticated identity cannot be reused\n- `tests/test_factory.py`: discovery, filtering, and deduplication behavior\n\n## Exit gate\n\nA test proves that an open non-draft PR is selected when it has `factory-review` or requests the factory account, while drafts, closed PRs, unrelated review requests, and an already-recorded `(PR, head SHA)` are skipped. Running `python -m unittest` passes.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nPublishing GitHub reviews, re-reviewing a changed head, monitoring CI, changing contributor branches, merging external PRs, and dashboard UI.",
