      "author_association": "OWNER",
      "body": "## Scope\n\nFor pull requests admitted by the opt-in review lane, run the configured `[review]` command against the PR diff at its recorded head SHA and publish the result as a real GitHub pull-request review. Map `VERDICT: APPROVE` to an approving review and `VERDICT: REVISE` to a request-changes review. Preserve the existing requirement that every finding cites `path:line`, and fail closed when output has no valid verdict.\n\nBlocked by: #5\n\n## Touches\n\n- `factory/dispatch.py`: external-PR review prompt, verdict handling, and `gh pr review` call\n- `tests/test_factory.py`: approve, request-changes, and malformed-output behavior\n\n## Exit gate\n\nTests prove that APPROVE submits one approving review, REVISE submits one changes-requested review containing cited findings, malformed output submits no approval, and each action is tied to the discovered head SHA. Running `python -m unittest` passes.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nPushing fixes to contributor branches, merging external PRs, CI readiness, repeated review after a new commit, and dashboard UI.",
