      "author_association": "OWNER",
      "body": "## Scope\n\nMake the review lane SHA-aware across dispatcher passes. After the factory requests changes, a newly pushed head SHA must become reviewable again; an unchanged SHA must not generate duplicate reviews. Bound automated review attempts with the existing `dispatch.review_rounds` policy and hand unresolved PRs to the human action queue with evidence instead of reviewing forever.\n\nBlocked by: #6\n\n## Touches\n\n- `factory/dispatch.py`: persisted review state, head-change transition, bounded rounds, and escalation event\n- `factory/dashboard.py`: action-queue data only if required to expose escalation\n- `tests/test_factory.py`: unchanged-head, changed-head, approval, and exhausted-round behavior\n\n## Exit gate\n\nTests prove that an unchanged head SHA is skipped, a changed SHA after REQUEST_CHANGES is reviewed once, approval ends the cycle, and exhausting configured review rounds records one escalation without another automated review. Running `python -m unittest` passes.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nEditing or pushing the contributor branch, interpreting CI results, merging external PRs, and rendering a dedicated dashboard review queue.",
